## Important decisions based on your structure

| Folder/file | Git decision |
|---|---|
| `src/` | Keep |
| `public/` | Keep |
| `server/src/` | Keep |
| `server/scripts/` | Keep |
| `server/package.json` | Keep |
| `server/package-lock.json` | Keep |
| Root `package.json` | Keep |
| Both `.env` files | Ignore |
| `node_modules/` | Ignore |
| `dist/` | Ignore |
| `public/robots.txt` | Keep |
| `public/sitemap.xml` | Keep |
| `src/assets/images/` | Keep |

**One important note:** Your `server/scripts/` and `server/src/scripts/` contain migration and seeding scripts. Keep these in Git because they are useful for future database maintenance.

## Before pushing to GitHub

Run these commands from the project root:

```powershell
git status
git check-ignore -v .env server/.env
```

Then check whether either environment file was already tracked:

```powershell
git ls-files .env server/.env
```

If either appears in the output, remove it from Git tracking (without deleting your local file):

```powershell
git rm --cached .env
git rm --cached server/.env
```

Finally:

```powershell
git add .
git status
```

Review the staged files before committing.

